1
00:01:02,813 --> 00:01:04,398
Managing Director Jun's day.

2
00:01:06,817 --> 00:01:08,194
Director Yoon Yi-jun.

3
00:01:08,903 --> 00:01:10,696
Someone once told me

4
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:15,159
that the superrich probably
only drink organic tea

5
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:16,744
served by their secretaries

6
00:01:16,827 --> 00:01:19,580
at just the right temperature and time.

7
00:01:21,749 --> 00:01:23,167
But that's not really my thing.

8
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:28,672
Instead, I start my day
with coffee I brew myself.

9
00:01:38,265 --> 00:01:39,308
Cut!

10
00:01:39,934 --> 00:01:41,685
Good work, sir.

11
00:01:41,769 --> 00:01:44,855
You really nailed that line. There, there.

12
00:01:44,939 --> 00:01:46,148
You can give it to me.

13
00:01:46,232 --> 00:01:48,192
You want me to drink

14
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:50,528
that burnt bean water and die young?

15
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:51,862
I told them beforehand,

16
00:01:51,946 --> 00:01:55,282
but over 70 percent of our employees drink
at least 1 cup of coffee a day.

17
00:01:55,366 --> 00:01:57,076
We needed to make it relatable.

18
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:58,452
-Bring me water.
-Water.

19
00:01:58,536 --> 00:02:00,204
Honey, I loved that wink.

20
00:02:00,287 --> 00:02:02,122
-You told me to wink.
-Right.

21
00:02:02,206 --> 00:02:04,917
But there's something
I forgot to teach you yesterday. This.

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,168
Get rid of him.

23
00:02:19,265 --> 00:02:22,351
The most important quality in a leader
is communication.

24
00:02:24,395 --> 00:02:25,229
Cut.

25
00:02:30,234 --> 00:02:31,986
I like all kinds of exercise.

26
00:02:32,069 --> 00:02:34,947
Soccer, basketball, baseball, and jok…

27
00:02:37,241 --> 00:02:38,409
Jok…

28
00:02:38,492 --> 00:02:40,035
BASEBALL, JOKGU

29
00:02:40,828 --> 00:02:43,038
Jokgu. I just love playing sports.

30
00:02:43,122 --> 00:02:46,584
Nothing beats playing sports
when it comes to building teamwork.

31
00:02:49,628 --> 00:02:51,130
It may not be anything special,

32
00:02:51,213 --> 00:02:55,092
but I'll show you the real me.

33
00:02:57,887 --> 00:02:58,846
I'm sorry, sir.

34
00:02:59,805 --> 00:03:01,807
Do you know why I make sure
to take herbal medicine,

35
00:03:01,891 --> 00:03:03,767
deer antler,
and wild ginseng every season?

36
00:03:03,851 --> 00:03:06,687
It's because I want to stay healthy
without breaking a sweat.

37
00:03:06,770 --> 00:03:07,813
Of course, sir.

38
00:03:07,897 --> 00:03:10,357
Find out who came up
with this stupid video.

39
00:03:11,025 --> 00:03:12,818
I want their exact name and position.

40
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:15,237
Because of Secretary Han

41
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:18,449
and the case,
the employees have been talking about you.

42
00:03:18,532 --> 00:03:20,284
The higher-ups are also unhappy.

43
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:23,245
You just have an interview left,
so be patient for 30 more minutes.

44
00:03:23,746 --> 00:03:25,080
Fine.

45
00:03:25,164 --> 00:03:28,000
He does hate having
Taekang's name dragged through the mud.

46
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:31,211
I had forgotten about that.

47
00:03:32,963 --> 00:03:36,050
I'm not sure, maybe lying?

48
00:03:37,384 --> 00:03:40,220
I can't lie, and I hate lying.

49
00:03:42,306 --> 00:03:45,768
Speaking of which,
I have never done anything

50
00:03:45,851 --> 00:03:49,438
that would jeopardize Taekang's future,
and I never will.

51
00:03:49,939 --> 00:03:51,065
What a load of crap.

52
00:03:53,567 --> 00:03:56,153
If he was so sincere,
why did he deny everything?

53
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:57,863
He's one hell of an actor.

54
00:03:58,614 --> 00:04:00,866
Of course, he's a great actor.

55
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:04,453
I can't say the same for you who has to
trick this guy starting tomorrow.

56
00:04:04,995 --> 00:04:06,872
Detective Kang is bold and quick-witted.

57
00:04:06,956 --> 00:04:08,916
She'll be fine
if she doesn't get riled up.

58
00:04:08,999 --> 00:04:11,085
That's the problem.
She keeps losing her temper.

59
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:12,419
-I don't--
-Hey.

60
00:04:12,503 --> 00:04:13,879
See that?

61
00:04:13,963 --> 00:04:15,923
When you act,

62
00:04:16,632 --> 00:04:20,427
you should be calm and restrained like me.

63
00:04:20,511 --> 00:04:22,388
You can't just go like this.

64
00:04:25,724 --> 00:04:27,101
Do you understand?

65
00:04:27,893 --> 00:04:28,727
Have you lost it?

66
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:30,854
Let's trust her.

67
00:04:33,649 --> 00:04:34,733
Watch me.

68
00:04:34,817 --> 00:04:38,946
The day we put handcuffs on his wrists,

69
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:42,116
I will reveal my true identity.

70
00:04:42,950 --> 00:04:45,369
I won't let myself get caught until then.

71
00:04:52,710 --> 00:04:54,211
MUSOE CLEANING

72
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:56,422
-Hello, sir. I'll be working as
-Jeez.

73
00:04:56,505 --> 00:04:59,091
-your secretary from today!
-Should I be the one doing this?

74
00:04:59,174 --> 00:05:00,884
I can't do it. I need to stay here.

75
00:05:01,385 --> 00:05:02,928
I'm not the youngest on the team.

76
00:05:03,012 --> 00:05:06,015
I really had to clean
because some woman was watching me.

77
00:05:06,098 --> 00:05:08,100
This could be a problem, Special Forces.

78
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:09,643
-What?
-Damn it.

79
00:05:09,727 --> 00:05:12,021
What? What's going on?

80
00:05:12,855 --> 00:05:16,608
I was afraid this might be the case.

81
00:05:17,568 --> 00:05:19,653
Don't tell me I've been caught.

82
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:30,414
You.

83
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:40,174
Busted.

84
00:05:44,511 --> 00:05:46,263
Did he figure us out already?

85
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:49,725
I think Yoon Yi-jun has the glasses cam.
Do you think he figured it out?

86
00:05:50,392 --> 00:05:51,477
Damn it.

87
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:56,190
Now that it's come to this,
there's no other option.

88
00:05:58,025 --> 00:06:00,069
I knew you were from the special forces,

89
00:06:02,154 --> 00:06:03,822
but look at your sense of fashion.

90
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:09,912
It's absolutely hideous.

91
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:12,664
What did you say?

92
00:06:12,748 --> 00:06:14,458
I'm Taekang through and through.

93
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:18,253
But if my secretary looks like this,

94
00:06:18,337 --> 00:06:20,297
what do you think will happen?

95
00:06:21,256 --> 00:06:24,218
My apologies, sir.
I ran out of contact lenses.

96
00:06:36,438 --> 00:06:40,109
I bet quite a few people had
the wrong idea about you in the military.

97
00:06:41,110 --> 00:06:44,113
Maybe they even asked you out.

98
00:06:46,824 --> 00:06:49,326
Has anyone told you that you are pretty?

99
00:06:50,452 --> 00:06:51,787
You are prettier than me, sir,

100
00:06:53,122 --> 00:06:54,206
with gorgeous features.

101
00:06:54,289 --> 00:06:56,834
Judging by how defensive you got,
I guess I'm right.

102
00:06:59,586 --> 00:07:01,755
How many flower buds are there
in that corner?

103
00:07:09,388 --> 00:07:10,597
I can't see well.

104
00:07:10,681 --> 00:07:12,432
You don't have great eyesight.

105
00:07:14,685 --> 00:07:15,936
Why are you…

106
00:07:18,105 --> 00:07:19,148
These aren't

107
00:07:21,650 --> 00:07:22,609
prescription glasses.

108
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:29,992
What are you hiding this time?

109
00:07:33,495 --> 00:07:34,913
What's going on?

110
00:07:35,414 --> 00:07:37,583
What's wrong with this?
Are we disconnected?

111
00:07:37,666 --> 00:07:38,917
The error isn't on our end.

112
00:07:39,001 --> 00:07:41,253
The target is a superrich murder suspect.

113
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:42,796
You got the bullets?

114
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:44,798
-Where's the bulletproof vest?
-Behind you.

115
00:07:47,217 --> 00:07:48,510
That punk is a lunatic.

116
00:07:48,594 --> 00:07:49,553
Put this on me.

117
00:07:51,013 --> 00:07:52,723
Nothing can stop the ensuing rampage

118
00:07:53,432 --> 00:07:54,766
if that punk loses it.

119
00:07:55,309 --> 00:07:56,768
Who are you talking about?

120
00:07:56,852 --> 00:07:58,270
Who do you think? Kang Jae-hee!

121
00:07:58,937 --> 00:08:00,480
What do I do?

122
00:08:07,154 --> 00:08:08,113
I did hide it.

123
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:12,201
I'm so tired of being called a girl.

124
00:08:12,826 --> 00:08:16,121
Since it's my first day here,
I wanted to make sure I look like a man.

125
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:20,250
I'm sorry.

126
00:08:21,835 --> 00:08:23,295
There won't be a second chance.

127
00:08:24,213 --> 00:08:25,214
Whatever it is,

128
00:08:27,174 --> 00:08:28,300
don't hide anything.

129
00:08:30,010 --> 00:08:30,969
Follow me.

130
00:08:38,435 --> 00:08:39,603
Damn it.

131
00:08:40,145 --> 00:08:41,730
That lunatic.

132
00:09:05,671 --> 00:09:07,089
I like how you react quickly.

133
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,342
Always stay on your toes.

134
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:15,889
You'll soon realize
how dangerous a place you've stepped into.

135
00:09:20,644 --> 00:09:22,980
He's crazier than I expected.

136
00:09:39,496 --> 00:09:40,330
A chandelier.

137
00:09:42,374 --> 00:09:43,333
The garden.

138
00:09:44,626 --> 00:09:45,836
The living room.

139
00:09:47,921 --> 00:09:48,922
The dining room.

140
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:53,802
The second floor has

141
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:57,097
one, two, and three rooms.

142
00:09:57,973 --> 00:09:59,349
There's a corridor there.

143
00:10:00,434 --> 00:10:01,310
All right.

144
00:10:08,066 --> 00:10:10,861
Sir, may I go wash my hands?

145
00:10:10,944 --> 00:10:12,195
Don't you need to eat,

146
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:16,658
drink, and breathe?

147
00:10:16,742 --> 00:10:18,618
Why don't you write a diary too?

148
00:10:19,202 --> 00:10:20,620
Don't ask me petty questions.

149
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:22,706
Yes, sir.

150
00:10:23,707 --> 00:10:24,750
Is this her?

151
00:10:25,709 --> 00:10:27,210
Choi Myeong-suk, the housekeeper.

152
00:10:27,878 --> 00:10:29,087
This way, please.

153
00:10:29,171 --> 00:10:30,213
All right.

154
00:10:36,303 --> 00:10:38,096
You're the new secretary, right?

155
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:39,306
Yes, ma'am.

156
00:10:39,389 --> 00:10:42,059
I'm in charge of housekeeping.
My name is Choi Myeong-suk.

157
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:44,895
Just call me Manager Choi.

158
00:10:44,978 --> 00:10:47,272
I'm Kang Jae-hee.
I look forward to working with you.

159
00:10:49,775 --> 00:10:51,443
He must've hired you for your looks.

160
00:10:53,945 --> 00:10:56,615
The two of you must really turn heads
wherever you go.

161
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,092
I must never let my guard down.

162
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:17,969
I need to search thoroughly.

163
00:11:26,770 --> 00:11:27,646
Oh, no.

164
00:11:27,729 --> 00:11:28,939
SEOK-JIN

165
00:11:29,856 --> 00:11:31,358
Are you okay? What happened?

166
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:32,776
I'm fine.

167
00:11:32,859 --> 00:11:35,904
But the camera isn't.

168
00:11:37,447 --> 00:11:38,740
I'm trying to make this work,

169
00:11:38,824 --> 00:11:40,909
but the Wi-Fi only catches
audio intermittently.

170
00:11:40,992 --> 00:11:43,286
It'll shut off in eight hours
if it's not charged.

171
00:11:44,121 --> 00:11:45,872
What about our captain? Is he there?

172
00:11:45,956 --> 00:11:47,749
We can't just keep this up.

173
00:11:47,833 --> 00:11:51,128
What are you going to do?
Are you going to do as you please?

174
00:11:51,211 --> 00:11:54,714
Yoon Yi-jun is extremely wary of people.

175
00:11:54,798 --> 00:11:56,591
I need to build trust first.

176
00:11:56,675 --> 00:11:58,802
-What?
-You're going to build rapport?

177
00:11:58,885 --> 00:12:02,013
A chance will come
when he lets his guard down.

178
00:12:02,097 --> 00:12:04,057
I'll make sure he shows his back to me.

179
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:06,101
Can you do it?

180
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:09,312
I'll prove myself
through my actions and results.

181
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:11,982
Don't worry and withdraw.
I'll complete the mission.

182
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:13,316
Solidarity!

183
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:14,484
Solidarity.

184
00:12:37,215 --> 00:12:38,467
Are you okay, sir?

185
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:40,510
Sir, are you all right?

186
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:43,096
My apologies, sir.
The cat suddenly jumped on me.

187
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:45,348
I didn't see you behind me. I'm so sorry.

188
00:12:46,850 --> 00:12:47,934
The sand on your face…

189
00:12:49,978 --> 00:12:51,605
Sir, I got new sand.

190
00:12:51,688 --> 00:12:53,064
My gosh!

191
00:12:54,483 --> 00:12:55,817
Sir.

192
00:13:20,008 --> 00:13:21,009
What do you want?

193
00:13:23,094 --> 00:13:24,638
EPISODE 2

194
00:13:36,191 --> 00:13:39,236
There, there. Did you miss Daddy?

195
00:13:39,319 --> 00:13:40,362
Come here.

196
00:13:41,321 --> 00:13:44,366
He's wary of people,
but he dotes on his cat.

197
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:48,954
Jerry, you also hate him?

198
00:13:49,496 --> 00:13:52,332
What did you say?
You'll avenge him for me?

199
00:13:52,415 --> 00:13:54,417
No, that's okay.

200
00:13:54,918 --> 00:13:59,130
I'm going to take him around
and show him hell.

201
00:14:01,007 --> 00:14:02,300
All right.

202
00:14:09,891 --> 00:14:13,395
I'll let it slide this time
since Jerry is also at fault.

203
00:14:13,478 --> 00:14:15,480
If you make the same mistake, I'll--

204
00:14:15,564 --> 00:14:16,648
It won't happen again.

205
00:14:17,899 --> 00:14:19,150
This is a warning.

206
00:14:19,901 --> 00:14:22,571
I'm not a very patient person.

207
00:14:25,448 --> 00:14:26,658
Did you get the handover?

208
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,952
Yes, from Secretary Jung.

209
00:14:29,035 --> 00:14:30,579
What do I dislike?

210
00:14:30,662 --> 00:14:32,205
Everything but what you like.

211
00:14:32,289 --> 00:14:34,583
-What do I like?
-Nothing.

212
00:14:36,418 --> 00:14:37,252
Correct.

213
00:14:38,336 --> 00:14:39,754
I'll change the question.

214
00:14:39,838 --> 00:14:42,257
What do I hate the most?

215
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:45,302
He extremely hates inefficiency.

216
00:14:45,385 --> 00:14:47,971
Whether it's a question or an answer,
only once.

217
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:50,599
You hate inefficiency the most.

218
00:14:51,808 --> 00:14:52,851
I also hate it.

219
00:14:52,934 --> 00:14:56,563
On that note, as a secretary
who is in charge of your safety,

220
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:58,732
may I take a look around the house?

221
00:15:11,494 --> 00:15:13,038
It's her, the Taekang Goddess.

222
00:15:13,121 --> 00:15:14,664
-She's beautiful.
-She's stunning.

223
00:15:14,748 --> 00:15:16,750
-No way.
-So pretty.

224
00:15:19,753 --> 00:15:21,463
She's the Taekang Goddess.

225
00:15:21,546 --> 00:15:23,340
She looks absolutely stunning.

226
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:45,362
Is Mr. Yoon's new secretary
coming to work today?

227
00:15:48,323 --> 00:15:50,116
Yes, I think so.

228
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:52,452
I thought he'd find
a replacement for Secretary Han.

229
00:15:52,535 --> 00:15:54,037
I'm not sure.

230
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,748
I guess Mr. Yoon has his reasons.

231
00:15:57,874 --> 00:16:00,585
I heard the VIPs are coming
to the chairman's office.

232
00:16:00,669 --> 00:16:01,711
Why?

233
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:04,506
I'm not sure.

234
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:08,259
I guess the chairman has his reasons.

235
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:17,644
Yoon Yi-jun.

236
00:16:18,395 --> 00:16:22,107
I need to build rapport with this lunatic.

237
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:24,567
All right.

238
00:16:26,194 --> 00:16:28,571
What? What's this?

239
00:16:38,665 --> 00:16:40,917
According to Secretary Han's family,

240
00:16:41,459 --> 00:16:43,211
it's likely that someone hid her phone.

241
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:49,676
Han Eun-young's missing phone.

242
00:16:49,759 --> 00:16:52,470
The forensics team couldn't find it
on the scene.

243
00:16:52,554 --> 00:16:54,013
It might still be in this house.

244
00:16:55,265 --> 00:16:56,307
What are you doing?

245
00:17:01,896 --> 00:17:02,981
What are you doing here?

246
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:05,734
I'm monitoring
in case you decide to slack off.

247
00:17:08,278 --> 00:17:09,654
How much do you know?

248
00:17:10,363 --> 00:17:12,115
I can tell that you're playing dumb.

249
00:17:14,784 --> 00:17:16,077
I heard there was a murder,

250
00:17:16,161 --> 00:17:18,413
and that you are the suspect.

251
00:17:18,496 --> 00:17:20,248
But you still came to work?

252
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:24,627
Secretary Jung ran away
the first chance he got.

253
00:17:26,129 --> 00:17:27,213
Aren't you scared?

254
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:29,674
I'm curious.

255
00:17:29,758 --> 00:17:30,884
You're curious?

256
00:17:32,343 --> 00:17:34,387
What are you so curious about?

257
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:37,098
Are you curious

258
00:17:37,932 --> 00:17:40,059
if I had really killed Secretary Han?

259
00:17:40,143 --> 00:17:45,523
Or whether I'm a cold-blooded
murderous psychopath the rumors say I am?

260
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:49,194
No.

261
00:17:50,779 --> 00:17:53,072
I'm curious why you hired
a personal secretary.

262
00:17:53,156 --> 00:17:56,075
Why now, of all times?

263
00:18:01,456 --> 00:18:02,499
Take five steps back.

264
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:04,584
Sir?

265
00:18:13,843 --> 00:18:16,137
You must follow three rules
as my personal secretary.

266
00:18:16,221 --> 00:18:18,223
Number one, keep your words efficient.

267
00:18:18,306 --> 00:18:21,810
Number two, keep a physical
and emotional distance from me.

268
00:18:22,685 --> 00:18:26,356
Of course, I can cross the line
whenever I want to.

269
00:18:26,439 --> 00:18:28,274
But you cannot.

270
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:29,943
If you do…

271
00:18:31,653 --> 00:18:33,863
Did Han Eun-young cross that line?

272
00:18:34,364 --> 00:18:36,616
Is that why you killed her?

273
00:18:43,081 --> 00:18:44,249
It's for your glasses.

274
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:45,875
It's fine, sir.

275
00:18:45,959 --> 00:18:47,544
Get a decent one.

276
00:18:53,925 --> 00:18:55,260
That damn lunatic.

277
00:19:01,307 --> 00:19:04,143
Han Eun-young wasn't on
any of the dashcam footage

278
00:19:04,227 --> 00:19:05,937
that Yoon Yi-jun submitted.

279
00:19:11,234 --> 00:19:15,238
But what if he didn't submit one
from one of his cars?

280
00:19:24,956 --> 00:19:26,332
What the hell?

281
00:19:28,001 --> 00:19:29,544
You are something else.

282
00:19:30,712 --> 00:19:32,463
You're foul-mouthed as well.

283
00:19:32,547 --> 00:19:34,465
I'm working, sir.

284
00:19:34,549 --> 00:19:36,843
I know, although it doesn't look like it.

285
00:19:38,469 --> 00:19:40,430
You'd know this if you got the handover.

286
00:19:40,513 --> 00:19:42,056
I don't trust people.

287
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:44,350
I will continue to keep my eyes on you.

288
00:19:44,434 --> 00:19:47,061
And you'll need to keep proving yourself.

289
00:19:47,145 --> 00:19:48,313
For how long?

290
00:19:48,855 --> 00:19:50,148
Will you trust me eventually?

291
00:19:50,231 --> 00:19:51,608
That depends on you.

292
00:19:53,109 --> 00:19:55,695
The final rule my personal secretary
must follow.

293
00:19:56,362 --> 00:19:59,782
There is one place you cannot go
in this house.

294
00:20:00,783 --> 00:20:02,660
Where is it? I'll keep it in mind.

295
00:20:05,622 --> 00:20:07,373
Second floor, last room on the left.

296
00:20:08,249 --> 00:20:09,626
You can't go in there.

297
00:20:10,418 --> 00:20:13,338
Okay. Second floor, last room on the left.

298
00:20:13,421 --> 00:20:14,422
That's the first…

299
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:20,678
Not good at memorizing, are you?

300
00:20:26,476 --> 00:20:27,644
Five steps back.

301
00:20:59,717 --> 00:21:00,718
What are you doing?

302
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:05,515
Look how sweet those two are
in broad daylight.

303
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:09,727
Look at you two. You must have hit it off.

304
00:21:09,811 --> 00:21:10,770
I can't believe it.

305
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:16,275
Nice to meet you.
I'm Kim Si-hyun from the legal team.

306
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:18,903
He's Yoon Yi-jun's closest confidant.

307
00:21:18,987 --> 00:21:20,196
Hello, I'm Kang Jae-hee.

308
00:21:21,197 --> 00:21:23,116
It's such an honor.

309
00:21:23,199 --> 00:21:26,202
This is the hand
that threw Mr. Yoon to the ground.

310
00:21:27,704 --> 00:21:29,706
-Who was thrown to the ground?
-You.

311
00:21:30,999 --> 00:21:33,126
-Who told you?
-Secretary Jung.

312
00:21:33,209 --> 00:21:35,503
They heard the thud
even from the secretary's office.

313
00:21:35,586 --> 00:21:38,047
I should've fired him before he quit.

314
00:21:38,131 --> 00:21:40,383
-How did you manage to do it?
-It wasn't too hard.

315
00:21:40,466 --> 00:21:41,884
It was part of the interview.

316
00:21:41,968 --> 00:21:44,637
I intended to learn
the deepest secrets of the candidate.

317
00:21:44,721 --> 00:21:47,098
-You use your back to do it.
-Do you understand

318
00:21:47,181 --> 00:21:48,766
-I see. What skill?
-what I'm saying?

319
00:21:48,850 --> 00:21:50,309
Like this. I'll show you.

320
00:21:51,519 --> 00:21:53,771
Take the other person's weight
and use your back.

321
00:21:53,855 --> 00:21:55,356
-Hey!
-Hey.

322
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:57,316
Watch. This is the important part.

323
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:58,943
-How do you do it?
-Do you get it?

324
00:21:59,027 --> 00:22:01,446
My gosh! Like that?

325
00:22:01,529 --> 00:22:03,448
That's how you threw him down.

326
00:22:07,869 --> 00:22:08,870
Stay.

327
00:22:11,414 --> 00:22:12,248
Jerry.

328
00:22:13,624 --> 00:22:15,668
Stay here with Special Forces.

329
00:22:23,843 --> 00:22:24,761
Your study?

330
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:36,939
Don't worry.

331
00:22:37,023 --> 00:22:40,860
I don't intend on befriending your master.

332
00:22:41,402 --> 00:22:46,157
You can love him
and receive his love all you want.

333
00:22:56,292 --> 00:22:59,212
The police already submitted
the autopsy certificate,

334
00:22:59,712 --> 00:23:01,547
and her body was handed over
to the family.

335
00:23:02,715 --> 00:23:04,217
We did everything we could.

336
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:06,594
As you said, we offered plenty,

337
00:23:08,054 --> 00:23:10,473
and negotiations with the family
are moving forward.

338
00:23:13,142 --> 00:23:14,185
So it was

339
00:23:15,645 --> 00:23:17,897
this easy to resolve after all.

340
00:23:21,692 --> 00:23:25,029
Kim Si-hyun wouldn't just drop by
during work hours.

341
00:23:29,367 --> 00:23:31,786
-Are you going upstairs?
-Yes.

342
00:23:31,869 --> 00:23:33,830
I'll take this to them.

343
00:23:33,913 --> 00:23:35,873
My gosh, thank you.

344
00:23:36,499 --> 00:23:39,627
So, when you go upstairs,
there's a door off to the left by itself.

345
00:23:39,710 --> 00:23:42,088
Whatever you do, don't go in there.

346
00:23:42,171 --> 00:23:45,550
May I ask why?

347
00:23:47,468 --> 00:23:49,220
Just in case I need to be extra careful.

348
00:23:51,139 --> 00:23:52,890
What's there for people like us to know?

349
00:23:52,974 --> 00:23:55,518
We just do what we're told to do.

350
00:23:56,978 --> 00:23:58,312
Thank you for taking the tea.

351
00:24:12,994 --> 00:24:14,328
Second floor, last room.

352
00:24:16,205 --> 00:24:19,542
There is one place you cannot go
in this house.

353
00:24:22,545 --> 00:24:24,213
Second floor, last room.

354
00:24:25,173 --> 00:24:26,299
You can't go in there.

355
00:24:27,008 --> 00:24:28,009
It's that room.

356
00:24:31,512 --> 00:24:32,889
Excuse me, I'm coming in.

357
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:43,900
So you just brushed off
my request to wait downstairs?

358
00:24:44,901 --> 00:24:47,820
Since you have a guest,
I thought I should bring tea.

359
00:24:47,904 --> 00:24:51,157
Insubordination from day one?

360
00:24:52,658 --> 00:24:53,743
There you go again.

361
00:24:56,871 --> 00:24:59,332
Forget it. Take it back.

362
00:25:00,958 --> 00:25:02,126
I'm sorry.

363
00:25:02,210 --> 00:25:03,586
I'll take it back.

364
00:25:03,669 --> 00:25:06,631
Please give them to me.
I'll drink them all.

365
00:25:08,799 --> 00:25:10,676
I like your tea.

366
00:25:10,760 --> 00:25:12,428
I'll be waiting downstairs.

367
00:25:18,809 --> 00:25:20,144
Why? Are you thirsty?

368
00:25:22,396 --> 00:25:23,773
What's with your lips?

369
00:25:23,856 --> 00:25:26,651
Cut it out. It makes you look ugly.

370
00:25:30,613 --> 00:25:33,282
-That day.
-Yes. I can hear them.

371
00:25:33,366 --> 00:25:34,659
What Secretary Han saw.

372
00:25:35,785 --> 00:25:38,913
How much has
Manager Park's side wrapped up?

373
00:25:38,996 --> 00:25:40,581
Manager Park?

374
00:25:40,665 --> 00:25:41,791
If…

375
00:25:42,291 --> 00:25:46,087
Secretary Han didn't see anything,
would things have changed?

376
00:25:48,214 --> 00:25:49,423
Han Eun-young

377
00:25:50,841 --> 00:25:52,843
saw something before she died?

378
00:25:54,136 --> 00:25:56,097
We can't change what happened.

379
00:25:57,139 --> 00:25:58,641
It's too late for hypotheticals.

380
00:26:01,143 --> 00:26:03,104
Sorry for making a pointless remark.

381
00:26:05,106 --> 00:26:07,024
How about the new secretary?
Do you like him?

382
00:26:10,736 --> 00:26:12,321
Not at all.

383
00:26:12,405 --> 00:26:13,781
Why not?

384
00:26:13,864 --> 00:26:15,533
You turned away your first choice.

385
00:26:16,867 --> 00:26:18,577
-He didn't have any.
-Any what?

386
00:26:21,289 --> 00:26:22,123
Conscience.

387
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:24,667
In the parking lot,

388
00:26:24,750 --> 00:26:28,087
it was obvious
the bereaved family was the victim.

389
00:26:28,170 --> 00:26:31,090
But he took my side
to get on my good side.

390
00:26:31,173 --> 00:26:32,341
That's why you hired him?

391
00:26:33,175 --> 00:26:35,094
You're cold inside and out.

392
00:26:35,177 --> 00:26:36,512
You're making me feel cold.

393
00:26:38,931 --> 00:26:40,433
Yoon Yi-jun is a piece of work.

394
00:26:47,690 --> 00:26:48,941
I'm leaving.

395
00:26:52,820 --> 00:26:54,155
Secretary Kang.

396
00:26:54,238 --> 00:26:55,906
You'll need to sign a formal contract.

397
00:26:56,490 --> 00:26:58,409
Please submit all the documents required.

398
00:26:58,492 --> 00:27:00,161
I'll handle your contract.

399
00:27:00,244 --> 00:27:01,537
Okay. I understand.

400
00:27:02,246 --> 00:27:03,748
I'll keep in touch.

401
00:27:03,831 --> 00:27:04,665
Got it.

402
00:27:05,416 --> 00:27:06,459
I'll keep my hands off.

403
00:27:07,335 --> 00:27:10,963
Right, you'll need to come
to the headquarters to sign the contract.

404
00:27:11,047 --> 00:27:13,174
-Is that okay?
-Yes, that's okay.

405
00:27:32,026 --> 00:27:33,652
Taekang Retail CEO Yoon Mi-jin

406
00:27:33,736 --> 00:27:35,696
and Executive Director Yoon Na-jung
are here.

407
00:27:47,583 --> 00:27:50,669
CHAIRMAN YOON TAE-SIK

408
00:28:01,597 --> 00:28:04,642
The promotional video was uploaded
at the perfect time.

409
00:28:04,725 --> 00:28:07,686
Yi-jun handled it well,
and so it was well received.

410
00:28:07,770 --> 00:28:08,938
What an attention seeker.

411
00:28:09,939 --> 00:28:12,358
I guess being on the delegation
wasn't enough for him.

412
00:28:15,403 --> 00:28:18,239
The rumors
are gradually fading away, Father.

413
00:28:18,322 --> 00:28:20,866
I think it'll be resolved
before the shareholder meeting.

414
00:28:26,956 --> 00:28:27,832
That's hot.

415
00:28:28,541 --> 00:28:29,750
Hey!

416
00:28:30,960 --> 00:28:33,629
You should've added an ice cube.
What's wrong with you?

417
00:28:36,924 --> 00:28:38,175
I'll go make another cup.

418
00:28:41,637 --> 00:28:42,680
You're smiling?

419
00:28:42,763 --> 00:28:45,057
I know you're going to spread rumors
behind my back.

420
00:28:45,141 --> 00:28:47,017
-Na-jung.
-What?

421
00:28:47,101 --> 00:28:48,978
Rumors are never baseless.

422
00:28:49,812 --> 00:28:51,981
Rumors only spread based on facts.

423
00:28:53,274 --> 00:28:55,776
I know Secretary Han
had something going on with Yi-jun.

424
00:28:56,652 --> 00:28:58,404
I'm telling you,

425
00:28:59,321 --> 00:29:00,197
there are rumors.

426
00:29:05,411 --> 00:29:07,580
The meeting is over. Everyone, get out.

427
00:29:11,917 --> 00:29:13,669
TAEKANG GROUP
CHAIRMAN'S OFFICE

428
00:29:16,547 --> 00:29:19,633
He's going to make Yi-jun the successor
despite the risks?

429
00:29:44,158 --> 00:29:46,785
There's no way the superintendent
would understand

430
00:29:46,869 --> 00:29:48,704
the fine taste of oven-baked bread.

431
00:29:48,787 --> 00:29:51,040
That's why we came here.

432
00:29:53,083 --> 00:29:56,629
Kim Si-hyun seemed quite fastidious.
Are you sure the documents are perfect?

433
00:29:56,712 --> 00:29:57,880
I get confused these days.

434
00:29:57,963 --> 00:30:01,050
Am I your servant,
someone you can order around?

435
00:30:01,133 --> 00:30:04,053
You're the only detective
who asks their captain to forge documents.

436
00:30:05,012 --> 00:30:07,223
I have no choice.
He wants to sign a contract.

437
00:30:07,306 --> 00:30:08,599
I can't get caught now.

438
00:30:09,350 --> 00:30:12,478
Whatever. What's Yoon Yi-jun like?

439
00:30:13,103 --> 00:30:14,396
He's a lunatic like no other.

440
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:16,899
His temper invites fists,
his tone calls for a beating,

441
00:30:16,982 --> 00:30:19,610
and his face
practically begs for a headlock.

442
00:30:20,194 --> 00:30:21,445
You'll beat him up soon.

443
00:30:21,987 --> 00:30:23,864
I can beat him up well. I can do it now.

444
00:30:23,948 --> 00:30:26,242
-What should I…
-Sit down.

445
00:30:26,325 --> 00:30:29,370
What happened to staying calm?
You said you'd build rapport.

446
00:30:29,453 --> 00:30:32,456
That's why I endured it all day
like winter survival training, sir.

447
00:30:32,540 --> 00:30:35,292
-Tell me I did a good job.
-You little…

448
00:30:35,376 --> 00:30:37,169
I said this wouldn't work.

449
00:30:37,253 --> 00:30:38,963
Good job, Kang Jae-hee. You held back.

450
00:30:40,047 --> 00:30:41,549
You want to see something funnier?

451
00:30:43,175 --> 00:30:45,010
He gave me this after breaking my glasses.

452
00:30:45,970 --> 00:30:48,514
Were there diamonds on the glasses?

453
00:30:48,597 --> 00:30:51,809
What's important is that Yoon Yi-jun
hasn't gone to the office in 15 days.

454
00:30:52,434 --> 00:30:54,019
That's when the incident took place.

455
00:30:57,815 --> 00:30:59,316
And Han Eun-young saw something.

456
00:31:00,484 --> 00:31:02,444
It sounds like
she wasn't supposed to see it.

457
00:31:02,528 --> 00:31:05,573
The first responders said
there was no evidence to justify that.

458
00:31:05,656 --> 00:31:07,866
Someone called Manager Park
took care of it.

459
00:31:08,450 --> 00:31:09,285
Manager Park?

460
00:31:12,621 --> 00:31:14,873
Did Detective Jung
go undercover successfully?

461
00:31:15,708 --> 00:31:17,126
He's the captain's trump card.

462
00:31:18,002 --> 00:31:18,836
Trump card?

463
00:31:24,508 --> 00:31:25,634
Damn it.

464
00:31:26,135 --> 00:31:28,429
Trump card, my foot!

465
00:31:35,227 --> 00:31:37,062
What am I doing here?

466
00:31:37,146 --> 00:31:40,357
All they do is poop, not gossip.
How am I supposed to get intel?

467
00:31:40,899 --> 00:31:43,319
-I am--
-Working overtime today as well.

468
00:31:44,069 --> 00:31:46,322
I know. Working late again.

469
00:31:46,405 --> 00:31:47,990
This is killing me.

470
00:31:49,366 --> 00:31:51,827
-Let's grab a drink after work.
-Okay.

471
00:31:52,995 --> 00:31:53,829
Hey.

472
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:57,082
I think Accounting Team 3
might get canned at this rate.

473
00:31:58,334 --> 00:32:01,128
The man who was handpicked
by Mr. Yoon is acting off.

474
00:32:01,211 --> 00:32:03,172
It's natural they're worried.

475
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:15,476
About Manager Park on Team 3…

476
00:32:15,976 --> 00:32:17,686
I heard he doesn't move from his seat.

477
00:32:17,770 --> 00:32:20,439
Apparently, he gets defensive
whenever you try to talk to him.

478
00:32:22,816 --> 00:32:23,942
Could it be that?

479
00:32:25,235 --> 00:32:26,195
What?

480
00:32:27,863 --> 00:32:29,198
Haven't you heard?

481
00:33:40,018 --> 00:33:42,187
I'm curious why you hired
a personal secretary.

482
00:33:42,688 --> 00:33:45,023
Why now, of all times?

483
00:34:10,299 --> 00:34:11,759
My gosh.

484
00:34:11,842 --> 00:34:14,303
-Are you okay?
-I'm sorry.

485
00:34:14,970 --> 00:34:17,222
-My bad.
-Are you all right?

486
00:34:19,641 --> 00:34:20,934
Are you Mr. Kang Jae-hee?

487
00:34:22,311 --> 00:34:24,480
Are you Mr. Yoon's new personal secretary?

488
00:34:25,355 --> 00:34:26,648
Yes, I am.

489
00:34:26,732 --> 00:34:28,358
I heard from Secretary Jung.

490
00:34:28,442 --> 00:34:30,944
I'm Lee Hye-jung,
Executive Secretary to the Chairman.

491
00:34:31,487 --> 00:34:33,030
I see. Hello.

492
00:34:34,281 --> 00:34:35,449
It's nice to meet you.

493
00:34:36,366 --> 00:34:38,952
Thank you for what you just did.

494
00:34:42,998 --> 00:34:44,374
She's the chairman's secretary.

495
00:34:45,250 --> 00:34:46,168
Lee Hye-jung.

496
00:34:49,546 --> 00:34:51,548
What a shame.
You've got a rough road ahead.

497
00:34:51,632 --> 00:34:52,800
Attorney Kim.

498
00:34:52,883 --> 00:34:54,968
Secretary Kang, you just became

499
00:34:55,052 --> 00:34:56,970
the public enemy of every man at Taekang.

500
00:34:57,638 --> 00:34:59,223
-What?
-They're all glaring at you.

501
00:34:59,306 --> 00:35:00,849
Gosh, that's hot.

502
00:35:01,391 --> 00:35:02,893
Their eyes are like lasers.

503
00:35:07,022 --> 00:35:08,607
Are they all looking at me?

504
00:35:08,690 --> 00:35:10,108
-Seriously?
-Who is he?

505
00:35:10,192 --> 00:35:11,985
-Who cares?
-Who does he think he is?

506
00:35:12,069 --> 00:35:13,153
Jeez.

507
00:35:15,656 --> 00:35:16,490
Can you let go?

508
00:35:19,660 --> 00:35:20,619
You must be nervous.

509
00:35:23,163 --> 00:35:24,706
Here at Taekang,

510
00:35:25,499 --> 00:35:27,960
there's one club you can't join
without shedding tears.

511
00:35:28,043 --> 00:35:29,586
It's called the LRA.

512
00:35:29,670 --> 00:35:32,005
It stands for
Lee Hye-jung Rejects' Alliance.

513
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:35,759
She must be popular.

514
00:35:35,843 --> 00:35:37,177
There are about 40 members,

515
00:35:37,261 --> 00:35:40,013
and around two men
join the club every month.

516
00:35:40,097 --> 00:35:43,350
Why? Because she regularly
rejects guys every time.

517
00:35:43,851 --> 00:35:46,895
I won't stop you
if you want to join the club,

518
00:35:46,979 --> 00:35:48,647
but I had to warn you.

519
00:35:49,648 --> 00:35:51,525
You must be in the club.

520
00:35:54,945 --> 00:35:57,531
-Why do you think so?
-Is it an unrequited love?

521
00:35:57,614 --> 00:35:58,657
What makes you think…

522
00:35:59,700 --> 00:36:02,244
Do you think I'd ever be unrequited
with this face?

523
00:36:05,747 --> 00:36:07,374
-I get it.
-No, you don't.

524
00:36:07,457 --> 00:36:09,334
That's not the tone I want to hear.

525
00:36:09,418 --> 00:36:10,752
Look me in the eyes.

526
00:36:10,836 --> 00:36:14,006
My pride is on the line here,
so let me make this clear.

527
00:36:14,798 --> 00:36:17,092
The Taekang Goddess may be pretty,

528
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:19,177
but I don't like her personality.

529
00:36:19,261 --> 00:36:22,180
She's way too flawless
and that's all there is to her.

530
00:36:22,264 --> 00:36:24,141
Why would I like her?

531
00:36:24,224 --> 00:36:26,810
Did you get that?
Why are you shaking your head?

532
00:36:27,352 --> 00:36:29,021
What? What are you…

533
00:36:37,738 --> 00:36:40,198
Secretary Jung told me
this is your first secretary job.

534
00:36:40,282 --> 00:36:42,743
-Yes.
-Call me if you need any help.

535
00:36:43,744 --> 00:36:45,287
Thank you.

536
00:36:45,996 --> 00:36:48,332
-And Attorney Kim.
-Yes?

537
00:36:49,333 --> 00:36:50,459
There's no need for that.

538
00:36:51,126 --> 00:36:53,837
I'd reject you anyway.

539
00:36:59,134 --> 00:37:00,886
-Good luck.
-What do you mean?

540
00:37:00,969 --> 00:37:03,138
Secretary Kang.
I wasn't rejected just now.

541
00:37:03,221 --> 00:37:04,681
Secretary Kang.

542
00:37:06,558 --> 00:37:07,601
It's urgent.

543
00:37:07,684 --> 00:37:10,312
Come to the men's restroom at the far end
past the elevator.

544
00:37:18,278 --> 00:37:20,739
The top part wasn't clean last time.

545
00:37:20,822 --> 00:37:21,657
-Here?
-Yes.

546
00:37:22,741 --> 00:37:23,700
Clean it thoroughly.

547
00:37:25,452 --> 00:37:26,912
Don't laugh at me!

548
00:37:27,788 --> 00:37:29,039
Come here!

549
00:37:29,122 --> 00:37:31,041
Don't stand by the urinal!

550
00:37:31,124 --> 00:37:32,709
I just cleaned it!

551
00:37:32,793 --> 00:37:34,294
It's good that you cleaned it.

552
00:37:34,378 --> 00:37:35,212
How's that good?

553
00:37:35,295 --> 00:37:37,965
You told me to ignore you
so we won't get caught.

554
00:37:38,048 --> 00:37:39,007
Why did you call me?

555
00:37:43,804 --> 00:37:47,557
Based on their conversation,
do you think Han Eun-young saw something?

556
00:37:48,558 --> 00:37:51,186
Yes. We already discussed this.

557
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:52,104
I'm leaving.

558
00:37:55,732 --> 00:37:56,900
There's one more thing.

559
00:37:57,734 --> 00:38:01,071
THE DAY OF THE INCIDENT
FEBRUARY 5TH, LATE AT NIGHT

560
00:38:03,156 --> 00:38:05,075
-What?
-Manager Park.

561
00:38:05,158 --> 00:38:06,451
Hey. Assistant Manager Ha.

562
00:38:07,619 --> 00:38:09,955
ACCOUNTING TEAM 3
MANAGER PARK MIN-HWAN

563
00:38:10,038 --> 00:38:12,082
I thought you had gone home.

564
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:14,376
I'm going to.

565
00:38:22,634 --> 00:38:24,386
Park Min-hwan from Accounting Team 3

566
00:38:24,469 --> 00:38:28,098
took something from Yoon Yi-jun's office
and went downstairs.

567
00:38:28,807 --> 00:38:30,267
He met his colleague then.

568
00:38:32,936 --> 00:38:35,647
We missed it
due to the malfunctioning CCTV cameras.

569
00:38:42,404 --> 00:38:45,323
Han Eun-young saw something she shouldn't,

570
00:38:45,866 --> 00:38:47,159
so Yoon Yi-jun killed her.

571
00:38:47,951 --> 00:38:52,998
And if Park Min-hwan took the evidence
from the office,

572
00:38:53,623 --> 00:38:54,624
it makes sense.

573
00:38:55,625 --> 00:38:56,752
Have you looked into him?

574
00:38:56,835 --> 00:38:59,337
He was hired by Yoon Yi-jun
when he studied abroad.

575
00:38:59,421 --> 00:39:02,049
The three of them were close,
including Attorney Kim.

576
00:39:03,633 --> 00:39:05,594
For the time being, tail Park Min-hwan.

577
00:39:05,677 --> 00:39:07,554
We need to corner him.

578
00:39:07,637 --> 00:39:09,139
The missing phone. That's the key.

579
00:39:25,072 --> 00:39:27,282
Mr. Yoon is feeling down today.

580
00:39:27,908 --> 00:39:28,950
Is that so?

581
00:39:29,034 --> 00:39:30,911
He's like that when he's sleep-deprived.

582
00:39:31,912 --> 00:39:33,371
It's happening often these days.

583
00:39:48,720 --> 00:39:50,097
Hello, sir.

584
00:39:51,139 --> 00:39:54,059
As reported, I was late
submitting documents to Attorney Kim.

585
00:39:55,352 --> 00:39:58,855
What is it now? Why are you on edge again?

586
00:40:01,983 --> 00:40:03,944
Did you touch the vase, sir?

587
00:40:04,611 --> 00:40:05,904
It has been turned.

588
00:40:07,322 --> 00:40:08,490
You can tell

589
00:40:09,407 --> 00:40:11,034
-that it's been turned?
-Yes.

590
00:40:11,660 --> 00:40:12,994
Yesterday, I put it down

591
00:40:14,079 --> 00:40:17,082
this way, not that way.

592
00:40:19,042 --> 00:40:20,043
Follow me.

593
00:40:21,962 --> 00:40:22,921
Now.

594
00:40:30,512 --> 00:40:33,181
It's gotten dimmer
than how it was when I left yesterday.

595
00:40:33,265 --> 00:40:35,892
It's definitely dimmer
than it was last night.

596
00:40:35,976 --> 00:40:37,602
So you can see those details.

597
00:40:38,812 --> 00:40:42,774
In other words,
I'm not going crazy, right?

598
00:40:47,070 --> 00:40:48,405
I'm hungry.

599
00:40:48,488 --> 00:40:50,073
I need to eat first.

600
00:40:59,332 --> 00:41:02,085
The Taekang Goddess
rejected him yesterday.

601
00:41:04,254 --> 00:41:06,006
No way. It's her.

602
00:41:06,089 --> 00:41:07,257
Attorney Cho.

603
00:41:07,799 --> 00:41:09,259
Will you be okay?

604
00:41:09,342 --> 00:41:11,553
-I'll get going first.
-Okay.

605
00:41:24,274 --> 00:41:25,233
Hye-jung.

606
00:41:27,444 --> 00:41:29,404
Everyone is talking about
how dreamy he is.

607
00:41:29,487 --> 00:41:30,572
Is he that handsome?

608
00:41:30,655 --> 00:41:33,116
I'm not sure. Is he?

609
00:41:33,950 --> 00:41:35,076
He looked pretty to me.

610
00:41:35,160 --> 00:41:37,245
So he's a pretty boy?

611
00:41:37,329 --> 00:41:39,831
It's rare for someone to be
both handsome and pretty.

612
00:41:40,290 --> 00:41:42,959
And that completes
the Three Handsome Men lineup.

613
00:41:43,668 --> 00:41:45,795
Yoon Yi-jun, Kim Si-hyun,
and Kang Jae-hee.

614
00:41:46,671 --> 00:41:48,298
You memorized their names?

615
00:41:48,381 --> 00:41:49,799
I like Managing Director Yoon.

616
00:41:49,883 --> 00:41:51,343
Who do you like out of the three?

617
00:41:56,389 --> 00:41:57,224
Secretary Lee.

618
00:41:58,016 --> 00:42:00,560
I apologize
for what happened this morning.

619
00:42:06,608 --> 00:42:07,901
I'm sorry.

620
00:42:17,327 --> 00:42:20,121
What did you say? Are you being serious?

621
00:42:21,081 --> 00:42:23,541
Yes, I am 100 percent serious.

622
00:42:23,625 --> 00:42:26,378
It means that
I trust you that much more now.

623
00:42:26,461 --> 00:42:29,422
What does that have to do
with this situation?

624
00:42:29,506 --> 00:42:30,382
Everything.

625
00:42:30,882 --> 00:42:34,177
My personal secretary just proved
that I'm perfectly normal.

626
00:42:34,261 --> 00:42:36,930
And you should take responsibility
for proving it.

627
00:42:37,013 --> 00:42:40,850
From now on,
you need to protect me even more.

628
00:42:40,934 --> 00:42:43,561
I'm already handling
both your executive duties and security.

629
00:42:43,645 --> 00:42:45,981
How am I supposed to protect you further?

630
00:42:46,064 --> 00:42:48,275
-Protect me from danger.
-Is that why

631
00:42:49,526 --> 00:42:51,236
you want me to be a food taster too?

632
00:42:53,321 --> 00:42:54,823
It's not part of my job.

633
00:42:54,906 --> 00:42:57,659
You'll get 200 percent extra hazard pay.

634
00:42:57,742 --> 00:43:00,704
Do you think I'd do anything for money?

635
00:43:00,787 --> 00:43:02,497
Yes, I do think that.

636
00:43:03,164 --> 00:43:04,249
You think it's poisoned?

637
00:43:05,125 --> 00:43:07,794
I heard you've been with Manager Choi
for ten years.

638
00:43:07,877 --> 00:43:09,254
As I told you,

639
00:43:09,337 --> 00:43:11,923
I don't trust people.
I only trust circumstances.

640
00:43:12,007 --> 00:43:13,216
Get out if you're not in.

641
00:43:35,280 --> 00:43:36,156
Are you crazy?

642
00:43:40,493 --> 00:43:41,911
You don't taste food like that.

643
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:44,331
What if something was in it?

644
00:43:51,880 --> 00:43:52,839
It's dangerous.

645
00:43:54,716 --> 00:43:56,384
You can have it all. Fine.

646
00:44:09,314 --> 00:44:11,399
-I knew it!
-Stay back!

647
00:44:12,359 --> 00:44:13,318
What's in it?

648
00:44:14,110 --> 00:44:14,986
What is it?

649
00:44:15,070 --> 00:44:17,822
-The food is…
-What did she do to the food?

650
00:44:17,906 --> 00:44:18,740
Tell me!

651
00:44:19,824 --> 00:44:21,951
Tell me! What is it?

652
00:44:23,119 --> 00:44:24,162
The food…

653
00:44:25,830 --> 00:44:26,873
The food…

654
00:44:26,956 --> 00:44:28,416
…tastes awful.

655
00:44:30,502 --> 00:44:32,253
This is torture.

656
00:44:32,337 --> 00:44:34,506
How do you eat this stuff?

657
00:44:35,006 --> 00:44:38,426
I add a small amount of Guérande salt,
Tuscan olive oil,

658
00:44:38,510 --> 00:44:40,804
Madagascar wild pepper,

659
00:44:40,887 --> 00:44:42,806
-and--
-I don't know what all that is.

660
00:44:42,889 --> 00:44:44,057
I can't test it like this.

661
00:44:48,603 --> 00:44:49,729
I will eat

662
00:44:50,772 --> 00:44:52,148
as I like it.

663
00:45:05,495 --> 00:45:06,454
It looks great.

664
00:45:09,290 --> 00:45:13,253
Isn't it pointless
unless the conditions are the same?

665
00:45:22,095 --> 00:45:24,681
-There's nothing wrong. Want a bite?
-No, I don't.

666
00:45:28,601 --> 00:45:29,686
MANAGER PARK MIN-HWAN

667
00:45:36,860 --> 00:45:37,819
Park Min-hwan?

668
00:45:39,279 --> 00:45:42,490
Do you think Park Min-hwan was
in charge of cleaning up?

669
00:45:43,408 --> 00:45:45,910
You know how the elites in films

670
00:45:45,994 --> 00:45:49,080
make their lackeys do their dirty work.

671
00:45:49,706 --> 00:45:50,665
He's here.

672
00:46:05,263 --> 00:46:06,598
Don't start the car now.

673
00:46:07,223 --> 00:46:08,808
Let's go. Start the car.

674
00:46:20,778 --> 00:46:22,071
Where is he headed?

675
00:46:22,155 --> 00:46:24,824
This isn't the way to his house.
Where is he going?

676
00:46:26,326 --> 00:46:27,452
It's Naon Art Center.

677
00:46:27,535 --> 00:46:28,828
Naon Art Center?

678
00:46:29,871 --> 00:46:30,914
I've heard of it.

679
00:46:36,961 --> 00:46:40,048
Get closer.
Change the lane and go after him.

680
00:46:42,342 --> 00:46:43,551
What's up with that car?

681
00:46:49,265 --> 00:46:51,017
It's hard, isn't it?

682
00:46:51,100 --> 00:46:52,810
It must be hard for you too.

683
00:46:53,478 --> 00:46:55,313
At least we're getting paid for it.

684
00:46:56,314 --> 00:46:58,107
He's been like that since he was little.

685
00:46:58,191 --> 00:47:00,735
He's always been a picky eater
with a small appetite.

686
00:47:02,570 --> 00:47:04,948
Just think of him
as an elementary school student.

687
00:47:34,477 --> 00:47:36,729
NAON ART CENTER

688
00:47:41,818 --> 00:47:44,612
No need. Wait for me in the car.

689
00:48:11,598 --> 00:48:12,473
Sir.

690
00:48:15,184 --> 00:48:17,854
You should've called me to your place.
There are CCTV cameras.

691
00:48:18,688 --> 00:48:19,856
I need to check something.

692
00:48:20,732 --> 00:48:22,734
The cameras are off,
so don't hang your head.

693
00:48:22,817 --> 00:48:24,193
It makes you look suspicious.

694
00:48:27,322 --> 00:48:28,406
Where's the director?

695
00:48:28,948 --> 00:48:30,491
She's on a business trip to Paris.

696
00:48:30,992 --> 00:48:31,951
In other words,

697
00:48:32,952 --> 00:48:35,747
no one else knows you're here
except for me.

698
00:48:40,793 --> 00:48:43,755
Did you destroy
everything Secretary Han saw?

699
00:48:45,048 --> 00:48:46,215
Yes, I did.

700
00:48:47,050 --> 00:48:48,926
Lie low for a while.

701
00:49:27,340 --> 00:49:30,134
I told you to wait in the car.

702
00:49:30,218 --> 00:49:32,804
Let me guess the reason you're here.

703
00:49:32,887 --> 00:49:34,806
Number one,
you needed to use the bathroom.

704
00:49:34,889 --> 00:49:36,683
Number two, you're lost.

705
00:49:36,766 --> 00:49:39,560
Number three, you're following me.

706
00:49:41,187 --> 00:49:42,355
I think I know the answer,

707
00:49:42,438 --> 00:49:46,401
but I think you're going to say
the wrong answer, Special Forces.

708
00:49:47,360 --> 00:49:48,486
Answer me.

709
00:49:52,824 --> 00:49:54,867
It's number three.

710
00:49:55,702 --> 00:49:57,954
Who are you? Who sent you?

711
00:50:02,625 --> 00:50:03,918
Damn it!

712
00:50:09,382 --> 00:50:10,800
Which news outlet are you with?

713
00:50:12,093 --> 00:50:13,386
I'll respond accordingly.

714
00:50:27,692 --> 00:50:30,194
I found him in the parking lot,
so I tailed him.

715
00:50:32,613 --> 00:50:33,865
I'll check the camera.

716
00:50:34,907 --> 00:50:36,242
-Or you can--
-It's fine.

717
00:50:39,454 --> 00:50:40,747
Wait for me in the car.

718
00:50:45,585 --> 00:50:46,878
I'll check the camera then.

719
00:51:49,065 --> 00:51:50,525
Cheers. Congratulations.

720
00:51:51,651 --> 00:51:52,819
It's your second time.

721
00:51:54,987 --> 00:51:58,115
Do you really want to get married
after that divorce?

722
00:51:58,199 --> 00:51:59,367
Of course.

723
00:51:59,951 --> 00:52:01,619
I didn't realize in my first marriage,

724
00:52:01,702 --> 00:52:04,914
but this time, I know she's the one.

725
00:52:04,997 --> 00:52:08,167
Marriage is great,
so you should all get married.

726
00:52:08,251 --> 00:52:09,502
Especially you, Kim Si-hyun.

727
00:52:10,753 --> 00:52:13,506
A divorce attorney supporting marriage?

728
00:52:13,589 --> 00:52:15,591
How paradoxical.

729
00:52:16,175 --> 00:52:18,386
How long do you think
you can keep this up?

730
00:52:19,178 --> 00:52:20,179
Forever?

731
00:52:21,013 --> 00:52:22,640
Welcome the women who come,

732
00:52:22,723 --> 00:52:25,226
and be glad when they leave.

733
00:52:25,309 --> 00:52:27,812
But what's the point of fooling around?

734
00:52:27,895 --> 00:52:31,315
If you're not sure, a settlement is better

735
00:52:31,399 --> 00:52:32,859
than useless evidence.

736
00:52:32,942 --> 00:52:35,736
I've settled things with myself
and decided I'll live like this.

737
00:52:35,820 --> 00:52:37,113
Let's drink.

738
00:52:37,196 --> 00:52:38,698
-Congratulations.
-Congratulations.

739
00:52:38,781 --> 00:52:40,199
-Thanks.
-Cheers.

740
00:52:41,200 --> 00:52:43,202
PROBLEM CHILD MR. YOON

741
00:52:43,286 --> 00:52:44,328
Excuse me.

742
00:52:45,496 --> 00:52:46,497
Hey, honey.

743
00:52:47,790 --> 00:52:49,208
About Special Forces…

744
00:52:49,292 --> 00:52:51,544
-Yes.
-By any chance,

745
00:52:53,546 --> 00:52:54,589
is the contract

746
00:52:55,089 --> 00:52:56,799
-finalized?
-Yes, why?

747
00:52:56,883 --> 00:52:58,217
Did you call me for that?

748
00:52:59,260 --> 00:53:01,929
Right, Special…

749
00:53:02,597 --> 00:53:05,099
Wait, why is it so loud?

750
00:53:05,182 --> 00:53:08,477
-Anyway, by any chance…
-I'll call you back.

751
00:53:08,561 --> 00:53:10,855
is Special Forces-- Hello?

752
00:53:11,731 --> 00:53:12,940
How dare he hang up?

753
00:53:23,326 --> 00:53:24,285
It's fine.

754
00:53:25,328 --> 00:53:27,622
Anyone would've gotten the wrong idea.

755
00:54:24,428 --> 00:54:26,097
You said I wasn't your type.

756
00:54:26,180 --> 00:54:27,974
And you aren't my type either.

757
00:54:28,057 --> 00:54:31,435
So let's keep this clean
and pretend we never saw each other.

758
00:54:36,691 --> 00:54:38,693
It's a little late for that.

759
00:54:39,360 --> 00:54:42,029
You're not who I thought you were.
Are you sure it's you?

760
00:54:42,113 --> 00:54:44,740
You're not Secretary Lee's sister
or someone who looks alike?

761
00:54:46,742 --> 00:54:49,286
If you're going to pretend
you don't know me, commit to it.

762
00:54:49,370 --> 00:54:51,622
If you want to party, we can hang out.

763
00:54:52,164 --> 00:54:54,625
I hate anything in between.

764
00:55:37,334 --> 00:55:40,671
I don't care if he's the suspect or not.
He's just insufferable.

765
00:55:40,755 --> 00:55:43,299
He's the very embodiment
of evil human nature.

766
00:55:44,008 --> 00:55:45,009
Good work today.

767
00:55:45,885 --> 00:55:48,721
But he's not from the Culture Desk
covering the exhibition,

768
00:55:48,804 --> 00:55:50,139
and the leak isn't from us.

769
00:55:51,098 --> 00:55:52,183
Then who is he?

770
00:55:52,850 --> 00:55:55,644
Things are going to get complicated
if the journalists catch on.

771
00:55:56,228 --> 00:55:58,355
What about Yoon Yi-jun?
Did he believe you?

772
00:55:58,439 --> 00:56:01,358
Right, it looks like he still trusts me.

773
00:56:01,442 --> 00:56:04,361
I don't know who he was,
but thanks to him, I didn't get caught.

774
00:56:04,445 --> 00:56:07,281
Seok-jin, what about Park Min-hwan?

775
00:56:07,364 --> 00:56:10,034
They met at the art exhibit,
so they must be connected.

776
00:56:11,285 --> 00:56:14,413
Captain wants evidence on Park Min-hwan
before the summons.

777
00:56:15,331 --> 00:56:17,041
Do you think you can find the phone?

778
00:56:17,666 --> 00:56:18,709
There's a room

779
00:56:19,335 --> 00:56:21,504
we're forbidden from entering.

780
00:56:22,129 --> 00:56:25,049
-I'll check that room out tomorrow.
-Okay.

781
00:56:32,056 --> 00:56:33,307
I noticed it earlier.

782
00:56:34,683 --> 00:56:35,643
Your button.

783
00:56:40,314 --> 00:56:41,440
Thanks, Seok-jin.

784
00:56:54,912 --> 00:56:56,413
-I can carry it for you.
-Thanks.

785
00:56:57,623 --> 00:56:58,582
By the way…

786
00:58:19,747 --> 00:58:21,457
I really don't want to go inside.

787
00:58:26,670 --> 00:58:29,715
I'm going to go into that last room
on the second floor.

788
00:58:31,258 --> 00:58:33,552
Can you be more gentle?

789
00:58:33,636 --> 00:58:35,304
That tree costs a fortune.

790
00:58:36,513 --> 00:58:37,973
Goodness.

791
00:58:38,891 --> 00:58:40,726
Good morning, Secretary Kang.

792
00:58:40,809 --> 00:58:42,186
Mr. Yoon isn't up yet.

793
00:58:42,269 --> 00:58:44,230
He didn't sleep well last night.

794
00:58:44,313 --> 00:58:45,689
Is that so?

795
00:58:45,773 --> 00:58:49,985
Could you take some water
and vegetable juice up to the bedroom?

796
00:58:50,069 --> 00:58:52,112
I meant to bring them up myself,

797
00:58:52,196 --> 00:58:54,782
but it's cleaning day,
and I've been so busy.

798
00:58:54,865 --> 00:58:57,159
Don't you worry. I can take it up.

799
00:58:57,243 --> 00:58:59,662
I have to wait until he wakes up anyway.

800
00:59:00,287 --> 00:59:01,497
Thank you so much.

801
00:59:03,374 --> 00:59:05,584
Not like that!

802
00:59:05,668 --> 00:59:07,878
The person before you did a great job.

803
00:59:14,385 --> 00:59:15,719
He's still sleeping.

804
00:59:15,803 --> 00:59:19,181
I need to get the camera glasses back
and check the room.

805
00:59:23,560 --> 00:59:24,853
I'm going in, sir.

806
00:59:58,846 --> 00:59:59,763
Sir?

807
01:00:02,182 --> 01:00:04,101
Wait, is he really sleeping?

808
01:00:06,395 --> 01:00:07,313
Sir.

809
01:00:16,697 --> 01:00:17,698
What on earth?

810
01:01:05,245 --> 01:01:06,246
Hey.

811
01:01:11,794 --> 01:01:13,420
I haven't called for you.

812
01:01:15,005 --> 01:01:17,549
I brought you drinks
on behalf of Manager Choi.

813
01:01:18,509 --> 01:01:20,052
I'll wait downstairs.

814
01:01:22,096 --> 01:01:23,138
Yesterday…

815
01:01:30,896 --> 01:01:33,148
At that place, I had…

816
01:01:34,525 --> 01:01:37,111
What about yesterday, sir?

817
01:01:39,321 --> 01:01:41,907
I think I had the wrong idea
at that place yesterday.

818
01:01:41,990 --> 01:01:44,410
But under the circumstances,
anyone would've done that.

819
01:01:45,911 --> 01:01:47,621
I'm listening. Keep going, sir.

820
01:01:47,704 --> 01:01:50,124
As I said,
I trust circumstances, not people.

821
01:01:50,207 --> 01:01:52,167
I simply trusted the circumstances.

822
01:01:52,251 --> 01:01:54,420
Do you understand what I'm saying?

823
01:01:54,503 --> 01:01:57,297
Yes, I'll leave and think about it.

824
01:01:57,381 --> 01:01:58,549
We can talk here

825
01:02:00,050 --> 01:02:02,261
since I've decided
to talk to you about it.

826
01:02:03,011 --> 01:02:04,012
Anyway…

827
01:02:14,773 --> 01:02:15,899
What I want to say is…

828
01:02:18,819 --> 01:02:20,237
The conclusion is that…

829
01:02:21,113 --> 01:02:22,448
Can you stop moving?

830
01:02:22,531 --> 01:02:23,449
I am sorry for--

831
01:02:23,532 --> 01:02:24,908
-I get it!
-Where are you going?

832
01:02:24,992 --> 01:02:26,618
-I'm talking to you!
-I said I get it!

833
01:03:43,737 --> 01:03:45,614
SPECIAL THANKS TO KIM DO-YOON

834
01:03:45,697 --> 01:03:47,449
He can't keep getting away with this.

835
01:03:47,533 --> 01:03:49,159
I'm the one who made her like that.

836
01:03:49,243 --> 01:03:50,702
Are you saying you did it, sir?

837
01:03:50,786 --> 01:03:53,330
She seems to hate only you.

838
01:03:53,413 --> 01:03:54,915
Watch over me until I fall asleep.

839
01:03:55,499 --> 01:03:56,917
Let's have dinner.

840
01:03:57,000 --> 01:03:58,794
You're full of surprises, Ms. Lee.

841
01:03:59,920 --> 01:04:02,548
Something is going on in this house
that I don't know about.

842
01:04:02,631 --> 01:04:04,591
Yoon Yi-jun's new secretary…

843
01:04:04,675 --> 01:04:06,176
I need to meet him.

844
01:04:06,260 --> 01:04:07,803
Weren't you in it for the money?

845
01:04:07,886 --> 01:04:09,846
-Found it.
-Turn the car around. Now!

846
01:04:09,930 --> 01:04:11,390
You're fired as of this moment.

847
01:04:11,473 --> 01:04:12,975
Get out of my house. Now!

848
01:04:16,770 --> 01:04:19,773
Translated by Leo Chung
